  "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#semiotic_projection_1",
  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the textual message as a recipient of reassurance",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the text 'don't worry' as the intended recipient of the message. The meme uses Nancy Pelosi's smiling expression (visual material) and the text 'don't worry' to create an impression that the user is being reassured or comforted by the speaker. The subsequent text 'we put an exclusion for white males...' is presented as the content of that reassurance, implying the user should accept this misleading claim as a comforting truth. The projection is onto the textual material, which acts as the direct address to the user.",
